hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"995","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani narrated to us, Khalid, meaning Ibn al-Harith, narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh bin Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, H. Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb narrated to us. Qabisah narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban bin Abdul Rahman, H. Muhammad bin Rafi’ narrated to us, Husayn bin Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, in the hadith of Khalid and Waki’, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, and in the hadith of Muadh bin Hisham, Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, and in the hadith of Shayban, he said: I heard Abu Salama, saying: He told me Jabir bin Abdullah said: Umar came on the day of the Trench and began cursing the infidels of Quraysh, so he said: By God, O Messenger of God, I had not prayed the afternoon prayer until... The sun was about to set, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, I have not prayed it.” So he went down to Buthan and performed ablution, then prayed. The afternoon prayer after the sun had set, then the Maghrib prayer after that.” The meaning of their hadiths is the same, and this is a comprehensive hadith."
